<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-3290] Unnecessary message &apos;IPython is available, use IPython for PySparkInterpreter&apos;</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3290</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When using IPython the following message is printed each and every time an IPython interpreter (%python or %pyspark) is started the first time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;IPython is available, use IPython for PySparkInterpreter&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I would expect to see&#160;only a message when ipython is configured but&#160;NOT working. Of course the error case message already exists, but this positive message is kind of annoying.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13142408">ZEPPELIN-3290</key>
