                            <comment id="16385428" author="aweise" created="Sun, 4 Mar 2018 23:16:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zjffdu&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zjffdu&quot;&gt;zjffdu&lt;/a&gt; is that message really required?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16385459" author="zjffdu" created="Mon, 5 Mar 2018 01:03:32 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The purpose of this message is just to tell user that they can use features of ipython. I will wait for other users&apos; feedback, will disable it if most of people don&apos;t like this kind of message.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16405453" author="tagar" created="Mon, 19 Mar 2018 21:09:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zjffdu&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zjffdu&quot;&gt;zjffdu&lt;/a&gt; I&apos;ve seen this warring for a couple of months now and I find it too distracting.&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
It would be best to report this to a backend log file rather than to users as a frontend message.&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
Not all our users would even know how to treat this warning, and what is ipython.&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
Most of folks that use Zeppelin know Spark / pySpark but not so much of internals.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16405651" author="zjffdu" created="Tue, 20 Mar 2018 00:39:27 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the feedback, will disable it. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16405752" author="tagar" created="Tue, 20 Mar 2018 03:30:14 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thank you &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=zjffdu&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;zjffdu&quot;&gt;zjffdu&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=aweise&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;aweise&quot;&gt;aweise&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
